WEBVTT

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:06.146
Buffer separates the React interface, normalized snapshots, and decimal scenario engine. Fixed

00:00:06.146 --> 00:00:11.942
server endpoints handle public provider reads; wallet keys and transaction signatures are

00:00:11.942 --> 00:00:12.908
never requested.

00:00:13.808 --> 00:00:19.801
Velocity validates mainnet accounts, markets, and oracle identity. Pacifica checks its public

00:00:19.801 --> 00:00:25.794
API's market identities and price timestamps. Jupiter validates position PDAs, ownership, pool,

00:00:25.794 --> 00:00:31.787
and collateral custody, but remains inventory-only. Its current prices and capped payoff

00:00:31.787 --> 00:00:35.283
are not modeled. Legacy Drift remains paused.

00:00:36.183 --> 00:00:42.386
For eligible linear positions, incremental price effect equals signed quantity, times frozen

00:00:42.386 --> 00:00:48.589
price, times the shock. Quote currencies stay separate: Velocity uses verified USDT;

00:00:48.589 --> 00:00:53.242
Pacifica price effects use USD. Sample denominations are illustrative.

00:00:54.142 --> 00:00:59.310
At minus ten percent, the four-market app sample totals positive one thousand

00:00:59.310 --> 00:01:04.477
USDC. The landing page's two-position sample totals positive three thousand five hundred.

00:01:04.477 --> 00:01:06.200
Both use fixed fixtures.

00:01:07.100 --> 00:01:13.000
Live snapshots expire within one hundred twenty seconds, sometimes sooner. Bounded reads,

00:01:13.000 --> 00:01:18.408
explicit errors, and request guards prevent stale calculations and late-account replacement.

00:01:19.308 --> 00:01:24.798
JSON reports preserve exact inputs and exclusions. Device reports stay separate from

00:01:24.798 --> 00:01:30.287
optional owner-protected cloud storage. Signup and recovery email remain gated. Private data

00:01:30.287 --> 00:01:32.117
bypasses the offline cache.

00:01:33.017 --> 00:01:38.452
Automated tests cover arithmetic, providers, storage, and real SDK behavior with mocked

00:01:38.452 --> 00:01:43.888
transport. Point-in-time mainnet reads are separate evidence; email delivery and native store

00:01:43.888 --> 00:01:45.700
packages are not claimed.
